{
  "_notes": [
    "World Poker Tour V1.40, all nine language sets. Upstream had no map for any WPT set.",
    "NVRAM fields were read from the ROM image by backport tools/samrom/samrom.py (adjustment ID n",
    "at 0x02102000 + 8n, the high-score descriptor table, the Master Volume setter, the score",
    "array literal), the rules validated on the mapped SAM games. All nine V1.40 images give",
    "identical addresses; V1.12 and earlier do not match the rules and are not claimed.",
    "Free Play is record 33 (ROM adjustment ID 34), Balls Per Game 30, Credit Limit 32: the offset-0 layout.",
    "current_player, current_ball and the status byte come from a headless libpinmame run of",
    "wpt_140a (two players, three balls, two tilts, 4 Hz samples of CPU RAM 0x30000-0x3FFFF and",
    "NVRAM): player and ball at 0x00033D0C/0x00033D0D, the only candidate the ROM offers and the",
    "only one the run found.",
    "Status byte 0x00033D38 (player + 0x2C, as on fg_1200af and potc_600af): 00 before the ROM",
    "initialises, 01 in attract and after the game, 12 with a ball in play, 14 from the tilt to",
    "the next ball, at both tilts. game_over is any value of 0 or 1; tilted is bit 0x04.",
    "Scores are 4 bytes on 8-byte centres from 0x02110A2C; bytes +4..+7 stayed zero after NVRAM",
    "initialisation. The champion records are the 32-byte form (checksum16 at +28), so the",
    "high scores are 4 bytes as well. No mode champions: the ROM's descriptor table lists GC and",
    "HS1-HS4 only.",
    "Master Volume 0x0211024C, 0-63, factory 40, complement check byte after it."
  ],
